From 28b2877ff33b8e53d30263f3b63a130dd2bab954 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:40:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/41] soc: qcom: mdt_loader: assemble an image as one
 contiguous blob

qcom_mdt_load() answers the remoteproc question: take an mdt and its segments
and scatter each one to its p_paddr inside a carveout. Not every consumer of
this format wants that. QSEECOM's application loader takes the image as a
single contiguous buffer -- the mdt followed by the segment payloads in
program-header order -- described by an mdt length and a total length.

For some images the program headers cannot be treated as a file layout at all.
In a Qualcomm-signed application seen in the wild, segment 0 declares p_offset
0, which overlaps the ELF and program headers being parsed, and two later
segments declare the same p_offset with different sizes. Concatenation in
program-header order is what the vendor's own loader does and what the secure
world accepts.

Add qcom_mdt_get_image_size() to size such a buffer and qcom_mdt_read_image()
to fill it, reusing the existing split-image handling rather than growing a
second parser elsewhere. No existing caller changes behaviour.

The symbol also gains a prompt. It was promptless because every user selected
it, and a consumer that must not select it -- selecting QCOM_SCM from a driver
that already depends on it closes a dependency cycle -- has no other way to ask
for it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
